          <g clip-path="url(#cyl-clip)"><rect class="hw-fill" x="986" y="168" width="72" height="130" fill="url(#hw-hot)" /></g>
          <rect x="986" y="168" width="72" height="130" rx="30" fill="none" stroke="#b87333" stroke-width="4" />
          <path d="M1000 186 q8 -6 16 0" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,0.35)" stroke-width="3" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" />
          <g class="tag hw-tag">
            <rect x="892" y="236" width="80" height="46" rx="10" />
            <text class="hw-head" x="932" y="254" text-anchor="middle">HOT WATER</text>
            <text class="hw-val t-cold" x="932" y="273" text-anchor="middle">off</text>
            <text class="hw-val t-boost" x="932" y="273" text-anchor="middle">30 min</text>
          </g>

          <!-- Snow on the ground -->
          <path d="M0 322 Q180 312 340 318 H1100 Q1280 310 1440 322 V360 H0 Z" fill="url(#snow)" />
          <text class="caption" x="720" y="345" text-anchor="middle">example home</text>
        </svg>

        <div class="wrap hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Open source · MIT · Unofficial · Model Context Protocol</p>
            <h1>Talk to your <span class="grad">Hive heating.</span></h1>
            <p class="lede">
              hive-mcp connects Claude and other AI assistants to Hive, British Gas's smart heating. Ask how warm the house is in plain
              English, and let the assistant boost the heating, put the hot water on or set holiday mode when you allow it.
            </p>
            <div class="cta">
              <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/getting-started/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
              <a class="btn ghost" href={GITHUB}>Star on GitHub</a>
            </div>
            <div class="pull">
              <code>docker pull ghcr.io/mattoddie/hive-mcp</code>
              <button class="copy" data-copy="docker pull ghcr.io/mattoddie/hive-mcp" aria-label="Copy command">Copy</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="chat" aria-label="Example conversation">
            <div class="chat-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><em>Claude · hive · writes on</em></div>
            <div class="chat-body" id="chat">
              <div class="msg user" data-step="0">It's freezing in here. What's the heating doing?</div>
              <div class="calls" data-step="1">
                <span class="call"><i></i>hive_get_heating<b>living room</b></span>
                <span class="call"><i></i>hive_get_hot_water</span>
              </div>
              <div class="msg bot" data-step="2">
                The living room is <mark>16.5 °C</mark>. The heating is on its schedule with a target of <mark>19 °C</mark>, so it's
                still catching up. The hot water is off until 06:30.
                Want me to give it a boost?
              </div>
              <div class="msg user" data-step="3">Boost it to 21° for an hour, and give me hot water for 30 minutes.</div>
              <div class="calls" data-step="4">
                <span class="call write"><i></i>hive_boost_heating<b>21 °C · 60 min</b></span>
                <span class="call write"><i></i>hive_boost_hot_water<b>30 min</b></span>
              </div>
              <div class="msg bot" data-step="5">
                Done. The heating is boosting to <mark>21 °C until 19:40</mark>, then goes back to its schedule, and the hot water
                is on for <mark>30 minutes</mark>, so a bath will be ready by 19:10. 🔥
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Stats -->
